    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Annunci,<div><br></div><div>I would recommend you to check on <a href=\"https://psu-psychology.github.io/psy-597-SEM/10_invariance_groups/invariance_groups_constraints.html#equality-constraints-in-sem\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://psu-psychology.github.io/psy-597-SEM/10_invariance_groups/invariance_groups_constraints.html%23equality-constraints-in-sem&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792421553293000&amp;usg=AOvVaw10gEfqQoNvF91P3OewC2lg\">this amazing post </a>by Michael Hallquist on this issue. On your second question, question, it says:</div><div><br></div><div><font size=\"2\">&quot;<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\">Circling back to our failure to corroborate strong invariance, we might wish to look at which constraints on the intercepts are leading to the greatest reduction in fit. Whereas the </span><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:2px 4px;color:rgb(102,102,102);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.04);border-radius:4px;white-space:pre\">modificationIndices</code><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"> in </span><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:2px 4px;color:rgb(102,102,102);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.04);border-radius:4px;white-space:pre\">lavaan</code><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"> gives information on change in model </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"><span role=\"presentation\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline;line-height:normal;word-spacing:normal;white-space:nowrap;float:none;direction:ltr;max-width:none;max-height:none;min-width:0px;min-height:0px\"><u></u><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;width:1.252em\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;width:1.01em;min-height:0px\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;width:1.01em;min-height:0px\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:STIXGeneral-Italic\">χ<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;overflow:hidden;min-height:1px;width:0.042em\"></span></span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;width:0px;min-height:3.994em\"></span></span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:STIXGeneral-Regular\">2</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;width:0px;min-height:3.994em\"></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;width:0px;min-height:2.381em\"></span></span></span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;border-left-style:solid;vertical-align:-0.297em;line-height:normal;overflow:hidden;width:0px;min-height:1.403em\"></span></span><u></u></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\">if we add additional parameters, we need to use the </span><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:2px 4px;color:rgb(102,102,102);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.04);border-radius:4px;white-space:pre\">lavTestScore</code><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"> function to examine how model </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"><span role=\"presentation\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline;line-height:normal;word-spacing:normal;white-space:nowrap;float:none;direction:ltr;max-width:none;max-height:none;min-width:0px;min-height:0px\"><u></u><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;width:1.252em\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;width:1.01em;min-height:0px\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;width:1.01em;min-height:0px\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:STIXGeneral-Italic\">χ<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;overflow:hidden;min-height:1px;width:0.042em\"></span></span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;width:0px;min-height:3.994em\"></span></span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:STIXGeneral-Regular\">2</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;width:0px;min-height:3.994em\"></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;line-height:normal;width:0px;min-height:2.381em\"></span></span></span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;border-left-style:solid;vertical-align:-0.297em;line-height:normal;overflow:hidden;width:0px;min-height:1.403em\"></span></span><u></u></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"> would improve if we freed (removed) these constraints.&quot;</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#666666\" face=\"Open Sans, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div>Now, on your particular questions: </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:1em;background-color:rgb(245,245,245);color:rgb(20,20,20)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:1em;background-color:rgb(245,245,245);color:rgb(20,20,20)\">To find the modification indices who advise me to remove the intercept of my item do I need to work on my metric invariance, right? Or on my scalar or partial strong model? </span></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font color=\"#141414\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">***I am not sure what you mean here. Metric (weak) invariance means constraining the loadings to be equal across groups, and allowing intercepts and means to be freely estimated. The intercepts are then fixed in scalar (strong) invariance. If the model has a bad change of fit (CFI delta &gt;= .01), then you can use lavTestScore to find which in which group could the intercepts be freed to have a better fit. If you free the intercepts for some groups but they remain fixed for others, then you achieved partial strong invariance (if the CFI delta is now &lt; .01). </font></div><div><font color=\"#141414\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#141414\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Does this answer your questions?</font></div><div><font color=\"#141414\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#141414\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Best,</font></div><div><font color=\"#141414\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#141414\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Alejandro<br></font></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Wednesday, 10 June 2020 17:11:26 UTC+2, Annunci Vendite  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color:rgb(20,20,20);font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Roboto,Oxygen,Ubuntu,Cantarell,&quot;Fira Sans&quot;,&quot;Droid Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:15px;background-color:rgb(254,254,254)\">Hi everyone,</span><br style=\"color:rgb(20,20,20);font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Roboto,Oxygen,Ubuntu,Cantarell,&quot;Fira Sans&quot;,&quot;Droid Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:15px;background-color:rgb(254,254,254)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(20,20,20);font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Roboto,Oxygen,Ubuntu,Cantarell,&quot;Fira Sans&quot;,&quot;Droid Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:15px;background-color:rgb(254,254,254)\">I need to find the modification indices of my partial strong invariance but I do have some questions about it, this is my code:</span><br><div><pre dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Roboto Mono&quot;,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;line-height:1.4;direction:ltr;color:rgb(20,20,20);background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><code style=\"font-family:inherit;font-size:1em\">model &lt;- &#39;\r\n\r\nF1 =~ item_1 + item__3 +item_4 + item_6 + item_9\r\nF2 =~ item_2 + item_5 + item_7 + item_8\r\n&#39;\r\n\r\n\r\nmodel_fit &lt;- cfa(model, data =my_data, meanstructure = TRUE)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nmetric &lt;- cfa(model, data=my_data, group = &quot;AGE&quot;,group.equal = c( &quot;loadings&quot;))\r\n\r\n\r\nmetric_mi &lt;- modificationindices(metric_age)\r\n\r\nmetric_mi</code></pre><pre dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,&quot;Roboto Mono&quot;,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace;line-height:1.4;direction:ltr;color:rgb(20,20,20);background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><code style=\"font-family:inherit;font-size:1em\"><br></code></pre><pre dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.4;direction:ltr;color:rgb(20,20,20);background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><code style=\"font-size:1em\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">These are my doubts: </font></code></pre><pre dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.4;direction:ltr;color:rgb(20,20,20);background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><code style=\"font-size:1em\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">To find the modification indices who advise me to remove the intercept of my item do I need to work on my metric invariance, right? Or on my scalar or partial strong model? </font></code></pre><pre dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.4;direction:ltr;color:rgb(20,20,20);background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><code style=\"font-size:1em\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Second doubt: is the modificationindices(metric_age) the correct way to find what I&#39;m looking for? Should I use lavtastscore(metric_age)? Than you all for your help</font><font face=\"inherit\"><br></font></code></pre></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
