     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><pre dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.4;direction:ltr;color:rgb(20,20,20);background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><code style=\"font-size:1em\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Should I use lavtastscore(metric_age)?</font></code></pre></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Yes, and you can search for previous posts on this forum for examples.  e.g., <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msg/lavaan/fzIg5jrxIAI/xoq5l803AAAJ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msg/lavaan/fzIg5jrxIAI/xoq5l803AAAJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792421553294000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3POBa4Qv0A8-vwuQoquSVo\">https://groups.google.com/d/msg/lavaan/fzIg5jrxIAI/xoq5l803AAAJ</a></div><div><br></div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792421553294000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0QlYFLTmUoV9oxrBxqCRmA\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div></div>"
